# Psalms of Solomon — Psalm 15 — The LOGOS Bible (Formal)
**Translator:** LOGOS | **Source:** Greek MS (Codex Vindobonensis) | **Section:** God the Refuge of the Poor and Devout

---

**15:1** When I was in distress I called upon the name of the LORD;
I cried to the God of Jacob, and he helped me.

**15:2** For you are the hope and refuge of the poor, O God;
who but you, O God, is the savior of the poor and weak?

**15:3** You will hear, O LORD, the prayer of the poor;
your words are righteous, O God, and you will not reject the hope of those who trust in you.

**15:4** When you are praised, who will have cause to fear?
For all that you have made will give you praise when you judge them.

**15:5** For the devout are in your hand;
it is your hand that saves, and you will never forsake them.

**15:6** For the fear of the LORD is upon the righteous;
they shall not stumble in darkness.

**15:7** The devout of the LORD will not fear the darkness;
they will worship with hymns, praising the name of their God.

**15:8** And the LORD will hear the prayer of those who love him;
he will not reject their petition when they cry.

**15:9** Blessed is the LORD who has mercy on those who truly love him.

**15:10** But sinners will be taken away into eternal destruction;
no memory of them will be found anymore.

**15:11** But the mercy of the LORD is upon those who love him in truth;
and the LORD will help his righteous ones.

**15:12** For our refuge is in the LORD our savior forever;
the righteous will not be shaken by the nations,

**15:13** but will walk in the fear of God,
for God is the champion of those who are weak.

---

*LOGOS notes: Formal English rendering following Greek syntax. Poetic lineation preserved.*
